**Finding: missing** (LOL-CAP, critical)

The Site Development and Hosting Agreement contains no limitation of liability at all. Targeted searches for "liability", "liable", "damages", "consequential" and "indemnif" surface nothing but the No Joint Venture boilerplate (p0061–p0062); the Warranties section (p0055–p0058) and General Provisions (p0059–p0070) are entirely silent on caps, damages exclusions or aggregate liability. There is likewise no indemnity anywhere to sit inside or outside a cap.

Consequence: both parties carry unlimited exposure, including consequential damages — well outside the fallback (mutual 12-month cap with carve-outs).

Redline (validated, ok:true): a new Section 9A inserted after p0058, at the preferred position:
- Mutual aggregate cap at the greater of 12 months' amounts paid or payable by the Company and USD 1,000,000 — the fee base (30% of Net Sales above $11,000/month under Section 3, p0019) is a real, non-illusory base;
- Mutual exclusion of indirect/consequential/punitive damages;
- Uncapped Excluded Claims: confidentiality/data protection/security, indemnification, gross negligence, willful misconduct, fraud, and infringement of the other party's IP;
- Company's Section 3 payment obligations expressly outside the cap.

Placement at the end of Section 9 means the clause inherits the existing two-year survival in Section 10.7 (p0068).
